Description: Tools for analyzing and interpreting distributed lag nonlinear models (DLNM) in epidemiological contexts. 
    Includes functions to simulate exposure scenarios, compute effect summaries, predict exposure-lag-response surfaces, 
    reduce DLNM effects to one dimension, and perform sensitivity analyses. 
    Designed for multi-variable environmental epidemiology with support for frequentist and Bayesian models.
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
